    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.attr_matrix - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.attr_matrix.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.attr_matrix()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get an adjacency matrix built from edge and node attributes.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.attr_matrix()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get an adjacency matrix built from edge and node attributes.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.attr_matrix()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Get an adjacency matrix built from edge and node attributes.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nGet an adjacency matrix built from edge and node attributes.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L93767-L93955){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.attr_matrix(\n    edge_attr=None,\n    node_attr=None,\n    normalized=False,\n    rc_order=None,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Attribute matrix](../assets/graphs/attr-matrix.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Two triangles joined by the edge C–D, with team x on A, B, C (teal) and team y on D, E, F (violet), and the 2 by 2 matrix of edge counts between the teams. Each triangle's three edges stay inside its team, 3 in each diagonal cell, and the single cross edge C–D (accent) puts 1 in each off-diagonal cell.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nEntry `[i][j]` adds up a value over the edges from the `i`-th row's nodes to the `j`-th\ncolumn's nodes. With `node_attr=None` the rows and columns are the nodes themselves, so\nthis is an adjacency matrix holding any edge attribute; with `node_attr=` they are the\nvalues of a node attribute, so the matrix tallies the edges (or their weights) between\ngroups of nodes, such as how many ties run within and between departments. Each edge\nadds its `edge_attr=` value (`1` by default, so entries count edges). On an undirected\ngraph the matrix is symmetric: each edge adds to both of its cells, a self-loop or an\nedge within one group to its diagonal cell once. Matches NetworkX's `attr_matrix()`.\n\nNetworkX returns only the matrix when `rc_order=` is given, and otherwise orders the rows\narbitrarily; EdgeCase always returns the matrix together with its row labels, sorted\nunless `rc_order=` fixes them.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[edge_attr]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[str, Callable[[rust.Edge], float], None]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   What each edge adds. If `None` (default), `1`. `\"weight\"` adds the edge weight (`1`\n    for an edge without one); any other string names an edge attribute, which every edge\n    must have. A function is called with each `Edge` and returns its value.\n\n<code>[node_attr]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[str, Callable[[rust.Node], Any], None]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   What labels the rows and columns. If `None` (default), the node IDs. A string names a\n    node attribute, which every node must have; a function is called with each `Node`\n    and returns its value.\n\n<code>[normalized]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, divide each row by its sum, so that row `i` gives the fraction of the\n    `i`-th row's edge value that goes to each column. Rows that sum to zero stay zero\n    (NetworkX gives NaN). Default is `False`.\n\n<code>[rc_order]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[list]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   The row and column labels, in order: node IDs or labels when `node_attr=` is `None`,\n    attribute values otherwise. Edges with an endpoint whose label isn't listed are left\n    out. If `None` (default), every label is used, sorted (by its text if the labels\n    can't be compared).\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [tuple[list[list[float]], list]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   `(matrix, labels)`: the square matrix as a list of rows, and the node IDs or\n    attribute values labelling its rows and columns.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If a node or edge lacks the named attribute, an edge's value isn't a number, or\n    `rc_order=` lists a label twice.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~adjacency_matrix`) \n\n:   The plain adjacency matrix of the nodes.\n\n[](`~attribute_mixing_matrix`) \n\n:   Count the edges between attribute values, as fractions.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nCount the ties within and between two teams, and the share of each team's ties that\nstay inside it:\n\n::: {#8dda6a84 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\"), (\"A\", \"C\")]\n)\ngraph.set_node_attrs(\n    \"team\", {1: \"red\", 2: \"red\", 3: \"blue\", 4: \"blue\"}\n)\n\ngraph.attr_matrix(node_attr=\"team\", rc_order=[\"red\", \"blue\"])\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n([[1.0, 2.0], [2.0, 1.0]], ['red', 'blue'])\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#a53147da .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ngraph.attr_matrix(\n    node_attr=\"team\", rc_order=[\"red\", \"blue\"], normalized=True\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n([[0.3333333333333333, 0.6666666666666666],\n  [0.6666666666666666, 0.3333333333333333]],\n ['red', 'blue'])\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Track times by zone\n\n`metro()` is a made-up city's metro network, each station placed at its `pos` on the map.\nCounting the tracks within and between the fare zones, and adding up their `minutes`,\nshows that no track runs between zones 1 and 3 or within zone 2, and that tracks get\nlonger from the center out, about 2 minutes apiece in zone 1 and over 5 in zone 3:\n\n::: {#30e6a1d0 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport polars as pl\n\nmetro = ec.metro()\ntracks, zones = metro.attr_matrix(node_attr=\"zone\")\nminutes, _ = metro.attr_matrix(node_attr=\"zone\", edge_attr=\"minutes\")\n\npl.DataFrame(\n    {\n        \"zones\": [f\"{a}-{b}\" for a in zones for b in zones if a <= b],\n        \"tracks\": [\n            tracks[i][j]\n            for i in range(3) for j in range(3) if i <= j\n        ],\n        \"minutes\": [\n            minutes[i][j]\n            for i in range(3) for j in range(3) if i <= j\n        ],\n    }\n).with_columns(\n    per_track=pl.when(pl.col(\"tracks\") > 0).then(\n        (pl.col(\"minutes\") / pl.col(\"tracks\")).round(1)\n    )\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (6, 4)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>zones</th><th>tracks</th><th>minutes</th><th>per_track</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>f64</td><td>f64</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;1-1&quot;</td><td>10.0</td><td>22.0</td><td>2.2</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;1-2&quot;</td><td>4.0</td><td>12.0</td><td>3.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;1-3&quot;</td><td>0.0</td><td>0.0</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;2-2&quot;</td><td>0.0</td><td>0.0</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;2-3&quot;</td><td>6.0</td><td>21.0</td><td>3.5</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;3-3&quot;</td><td>5.0</td><td>27.0</td><td>5.4</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#35289552 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro.plot(layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"zone\", label_by=\"label\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de